/*  FUNCTION NAME:      ADDRESSES
    DESCRIPTION:*//**Returns the A1-style addresses of cells in a range as text, shape-matching the input range.*/
/*  RETURNS:            array of address (text), relative A1 form, same shape as the input range
    PARAMETERS:
        cells           (Required) A cell or range reference. Output shape matches the input shape. Addresses are returned in relative form (no $ anchors), matching TOPOS / MOVECELL / POSTOCELL conventions.
    EXAMPLE:            =ADDRESSES(F28:H30) -> 3x3 grid of "F28" through "H30"
    REVISIONS:          Date        Developer   Description
                        2026-05-20  Claude      Initial version
                        2026-11-09  Claude      Help table removed from the formula; its text is the header metadata the argument hints read (#381, #382)
*/
ADDRESSES = LAMBDA(
//  Parameter Declarations
    [cells],
    LET(
    //  Procedure
        result, ADDRESS(ROW(cells), COLUMN(cells), 4),
        result
)
);
